  "question": {
    "text": "Let $L$ be a normal to the parabola $y^2=4 x$. If $L$ passes through the point $(9,6)$, then $L$ is given by",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "nQHsQ",
      "text": "\n$y-x+3=0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "I78qB",
      "text": "\n$y+3 x-33=0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "1Gj9n",
      "text": "\n$y+x-15=0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "KYIQ4",
      "text": "\n$y-2 x+12=0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Normal to $y^2=4 x$, is $y-m x-2 m-m^3$ which passes through $(9,6)$.\nNow, $\\quad 6=9 m-2 m-m^3$ $\\Rightarrow m^3-7 m+6=0 \\Rightarrow m=1,2,-3$\n$\\therefore$ Equation of normals are\n$y-x+3=0$\n$y+3 x-33=0$ and $y-2 x+12=0$",
    "image": null
  },
